      "s": "TechCrunch",
      "t": "Waymo starts offering rides at the Las Vegas airport",
      "d": "Waymo only just started offering rides to the public in Las Vegas in September but is already serving a 24-square-mile area in the city.",
      "u": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/21/waymo-starts-offering-rides-at-the-las-vegas-airport/",
      "m": "10. 21. PM 04:59",
      "ts": 1792601984000,
      "fullText": "In Brief Posted: 9:59 AM PDT · October 21, 2026 Image Credits: Waymo Sean O&#039;Kane Waymo starts offering rides at the Las Vegas airport Waymo is now shuttling customers to and from the Harry Reid International Airport in Las Vegas, with pickups and drop-offs happening at dedicated &#8220;autonomous vehicle zones&#8221; at Terminal 1 and Terminal 3, the company announced Wednesday. This is the sixth major airport that Waymo is serving. The company already offers rides at Phoenix Sky Harbor, Nashville International, San Antonio International, San Francisco International, and San José International airports. Waymo only just started offering rides to the public in Las Vegas in September but is already serving a 24-square-mile area in the city. The company said the rides to and from the Las Vegas airport will be limited at first to just a few riders, before opening up to all customers. Amazon-owned Zoox already offers rides at the Vegas airport, and more robotaxis are coming to Sin City. In August, state regulators approved permits that will allow Tesla and Uber to put thousands of them on the city&#8217;s streets in the next year. Topics autonomous vehicles , In Brief , robotaxis , Transportation , Waymo November 4 Boston Buy One Pass, Get a Second Free Cover more ground at TechCrunch&#8217;s ultimate founder bootcamp of the year by bringing your co-founder or partner for free Book before the BOGO deal expires Register Now Newsletters See More Subscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news TechCrunch Daily News Every weekday and Sunday, you can get the best of TechCrunch’s coverage. TechCrunch Mobility TechCrunch Mobility is your destination for transportation news and insight. Startups Weekly Startups are the core of TechCrunch, so get our best coverage delivered weekly. StrictlyVC Provides movers and shakers with the info they need to start their day. No newsletters selected. Subscribe By submitting your email, you agree to our Terms and Privacy 